# What the daemon does not need in order to build this image.
#
# There was no such file, and the build context was 1.39 GB: `web/node_modules`
# (608 MB), `web/.next` (785 MB) and whatever `data/` happens to hold — on a machine
# that has run `make ingest`, gigabytes of video. CI never noticed, because a fresh
# checkout has none of those; it is only ever slow for the person who actually
# develops here, which is the worst place for the cost to land.
#
# It also defeated the layering the Dockerfile is careful about. `COPY web/ ./`
# copied a host node_modules into the builder immediately after `npm ci` had
# installed the right one, so the "dependencies before source" split bought nothing.

# --- the two that made the context a gigabyte ---
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/out

# --- datasets, working copies and downloads ---
# The image reads a dataset from a mount or a URI. It never carries one.
data/
*.lance/

# --- build outputs that are not this image ---
dist/
build/
desktop/target/
desktop/src-tauri/target/
packaging/build/
packaging/dist/
*.dmg
*.app

# --- python ephemera ---
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- secrets and local configuration, none of which belong in a build context ---
.cred
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- vcs, editors, CI ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# docs/ is deliberately NOT excluded: docker/Dockerfile copies docs/guide/ into the
# web stage, because app/lib/docs.ts resolves the guide at `../docs/guide` and an
# empty generateStaticParams is a build error under `output: export`.
